From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:15:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] answer getTPS at server scope when the caller is off-region

CraftServer#getTPS and #getAverageTickTime resolve the region the calling
thread is ticking, and fail if they cannot. Both halves of that are wrong here,
and the half that succeeds is the worse one.

It throws. Paper's contract has no failure mode for either method - they read a
statistic, touch no world state and need no ownership - so every caller off a
tick thread dies with UnsupportedOperationException("Not on any region"). That
is not only plugins: this fork's own console GUI calls getTPS from a Swing timer
on the AWT event thread, unguarded, in two places (RAMDetails#update and
StatsComponent#tick), so a server started with a GUI throws twice a second.

It lies. Folia's global tick handle is a RegionScheduleHandle like any other, so
a caller on the global region thread resolves it and is handed the global tick's
own TPS. The global tick advances weather, the world border and connections and
nothing else, so it sits at 20.00 however far behind the worlds are. Console and
RCON commands run on the global region, which means an operator running any
plugin's /tps from the console is told the server is healthy while every region
crawls, and the common "restart when TPS drops below X" timer, scheduled on the
global scheduler, never fires. A number that is always healthy is worse than an
exception, because nothing reports it as broken.

Measured on the A/B pair, no players, both cores idle: Paper's /tps prints
20.0/20.0/20.0 and Folia's region-aware /tps prints 19.87 for the one live
region - so the platform already knows the honest figure; it is only the Bukkit
server-scope accessor that does not report it.

Only the off-region answer changes. A caller on a world region thread still gets
that region's figures, which is Folia's deliberate design and the better answer
to a player-scoped question. Every other caller - global region thread, shutdown
thread with no region, GUI thread, a plugin's own pool - gets the worst world
region, which is the same figure the platform's own /tps prints first as "Lowest
Region TPS". A mean or a median would hide exactly the region being asked about.

The predicate is getCurrentRegion() == null rather than the platform's
instanceof test, because that is the precise difference: the global tick handle
satisfies the instanceof and is what produces the constant 20.00.

A region with no tick report yet is skipped rather than counted as 20.00; with
no world region at all the configured tick rate is returned, which is honest -
nothing is behind because nothing is running.

No information is lost by making a server-scope method answer at server scope:
Server#getRegionTPS(World, int, int) and its Location/Chunk overloads already
answer the per-region question, from any thread.

Kill switch: compat-config.server-tps-off-region=false.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
index 6597649f8c8afd8c89c67ba28a7fc49b5f73e2c2..5295369735bbb7b4241fbb723ec5574e2353aaa1 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
@@ -2811,6 +2811,13 @@ public final class CraftServer implements Server {
 
     @Override
     public double getAverageTickTime() {
+        // Lecithin start - same gap as getTPS above: the worst region's tick time, rather than the
+        // global tick's or an exception, when the caller is not inside a world region.
+        final Long lecithinServerWide = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinServerTps.getAverageTickTimeNanos();
+        if (lecithinServerWide != null) {
+            return lecithinServerWide.longValue() / 1.0E6;
+        }
+        // Lecithin end
         // Folia start - region threading
         ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.scheduler.SchedulableTick task = io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.TickRegionScheduler.getCurrentTickingTask();
         if (task == null) {
@@ -2884,6 +2891,15 @@ public final class CraftServer implements Server {
 
     @Override
     public double[] getTPS() {
+        // Lecithin start - answer at server scope when the caller is not inside a world region.
+        // Stock resolves the global tick handle on the global region thread, which reports 20.00
+        // whatever the worlds are doing, and throws on every other thread including the fork's own
+        // GUI timer. See LecithinServerTps.
+        final double[] lecithinServerWide = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinServerTps.getTPS();
+        if (lecithinServerWide != null) {
+            return lecithinServerWide;
+        }
+        // Lecithin end
         // Folia start - region threading
         ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.scheduler.SchedulableTick task = io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.TickRegionScheduler.getCurrentTickingTask();
         if (task == null) {
